ok - pipeline admission preserves count/load boundaries, priority, start registration, timing and descriptor ownership
ok - pool size follows the host CPU count
ok - run returns the command's status and marks the child with its exact count
ok - invalid reservations refuse work in both option forms, including nested calls
ok - passes are exclusive, waiters queue, and notices stay off the command's output
ok - a multi-pass request keeps collected passes and runs once it holds all
ok - owner death releases passes without inherited child lock copies
ok - failure cleanup terminates and reaps wrappers and their workloads
ok - a TERM to the holder keeps the pass until the running command ends
ok - a waiter ended while queued exits without running its command
ok - nested runs execute under the outer reservation
ok - an unusable pool or missing python3 runs the command without a pass and says so
ok - no-Python execution rejects invalid counts and preserves valid degraded work
ok - inherited markers are validated consistently while degraded work still runs
ok - the runner takes each script's pass outside its bound and keeps notices off script output
ok - nested runners take no new pass and limit scripts to the inherited reservation
